The version-pinned patch changes only Android-host behavior:
1. skip Flutter's normal cache updater because it has no Android host artifact set;
2. read the hash-checked flutter.version.json instead of refreshing version data with Git;
3. calculate the display-only framework age from frameworkCommitDate without Git.

A fail-closed Git compatibility shim is bundled because Flutter requires a Git
executable to be discoverable during startup. It exits 69 if invoked and never
fabricates Git output. A logging probe confirmed it was not invoked by the
successful version/create/pub sequence.

