RESULT
PASS: The standalone Android app installed a hash-checked, version-pinned
Flutter tool bundle from its APK, linked it to the separately installed native
Android/ARM64 Dart SDK, ran `flutter --version`, generated an Android Flutter
project, resolved and downloaded Pub packages, populated its private Pub cache,
then resolved the same dependencies offline. It reused both toolchains on the
next app launch.

LIMIT OF THIS RESULT
This does not yet prove `flutter doctor`, Java/Gradle execution, Flutter front-
end compilation of an application, engine artifact use, AAPT2/D8 packaging,
APK signing, or installation of a newly generated Flutter APK. Those require
the next Android build-toolchain milestone. The installed APK in this proof was
built on the development host and only contains the on-device probes.
